<title>FRANCE: Suez 1996 turnover 56.7 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Suez 1996 turnover 56.7 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					56,708    vs   53,515</p>
<p>	- Ste Generale de Belgique	    27,028    vs   28,085</p>
<p>	- specialised financial units	 21,971    vs   17,892</p>
<p>	- Credisuez				  6,232    vs    6,349</p>
<p>	- Compagnie de Suez and others	 1,477    vs    1,189</p>
<p>NOTE - Suez made the announcment in the official bulletin Balo. It said that the figures were on a like-for-like basis, excluding Indosuez after its sale to Credit Agricole. On a constant structure and unchanged consolidation method, sales rose six percent over 1995. The fall recorded at Societe Generale de Belgique stems mainly from an unfavourable Belgian franc/French franc parity.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
